WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:05.866
- For the entrepreneur
who's getting started,

00:00:05.866 --> 00:00:07.847
and trying to build this
to a full time business,

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:09.839
or for the entrepreneur
who's already in a full time

00:00:09.839 --> 00:00:11.167
and tryin' to get to that next step,

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.431
what are some of the tips that you

00:00:12.431 --> 00:00:14.840
would give them on how to be productive?

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.648
- Well, I often ask my entrepreneurs,

00:00:17.648 --> 00:00:19.335
I say, why do you get up and go to bed

00:00:19.335 --> 00:00:21.988
in the morning, go to work in the morning?

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:22.829
Why do you get out of bed?

00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:25.104
And they say, they think
about it for a while,

00:00:25.104 --> 00:00:27.321
and I say, well, the answer is MMM,

00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:29.403
which means make more money.

00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:31.260
You don't go to work to make less money,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.201
or to make the same money, you go to bed,

00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:35.154
you go to work to make more money.

00:00:35.154 --> 00:00:36.926
So I say, now how do you make more money?

00:00:36.926 --> 00:00:41.808
Well, it's called SMS, and
that means sell more stuff.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.558
And, then, so, you MMM by SMSing.

00:00:45.424 --> 00:00:47.405
Now, if you are not selling more stuff

00:00:47.405 --> 00:00:49.603
in the course of the day, then
you might was well go home

00:00:49.603 --> 00:00:52.394
to bed, covers up over your
head, and go back to sleep,

00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:55.135
because you're of no value
to yourself or anyone else.

00:00:55.135 --> 00:00:57.035
And then I start to point out,

00:00:57.035 --> 00:00:59.716
I notice, I learned this
from a very successful man,

00:00:59.716 --> 00:01:02.147
look around your office, all
right, look around your office.

00:01:02.147 --> 00:01:03.672
Now, what don't you see in your office?

00:01:03.672 --> 00:01:06.750
And the answer is, you don't
see any customers, all right.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.898
So, why are you in your office?

00:01:08.898 --> 00:01:11.979
There's no customers there,
you can't sell more stuff,

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:13.337
and if you think you're
going to sell more stuff

00:01:13.337 --> 00:01:16.002
by sending out tricky email messages,

00:01:16.002 --> 00:01:19.556
then you probably need some medication,

00:01:19.556 --> 00:01:21.443
or a check up from the neck up.

00:01:21.443 --> 00:01:23.670
The only way that sell
stuff is you go out there

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.642
and you talk to customers
and you ask them to buy it.

00:01:26.642 --> 00:01:28.103
And, so, if you're not
out asking to buy it.

00:01:28.103 --> 00:01:31.048
Now, what are the three
keys to selling more stuff?

00:01:31.048 --> 00:01:33.704
They are prospecting,
presenting, and closing.

00:01:33.704 --> 00:01:36.068
Prospecting means finding new people

00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:39.753
who can and will buy and pay
in a short period of time,

00:01:39.753 --> 00:01:42.052
and then telling them, presenting,

00:01:42.052 --> 00:01:43.909
that your product or
service, and why it is

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:46.322
the very best choice for them now,

00:01:46.322 --> 00:01:47.676
and then closing them, and getting 'em

00:01:47.676 --> 00:01:50.589
to make a decision today, this minute.

00:01:50.589 --> 00:01:53.900
So, therefore, that all come
together, is prospecting,

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.588
presenting and closing is
how you sell more stuff,

00:01:56.588 --> 00:01:59.091
which is why you got out
of bed in the first place.

00:01:59.091 --> 00:02:02.077
Now, so the interview,
the interesting point

00:02:02.077 --> 00:02:04.105
'cause I've been through
all of this myself,

00:02:04.105 --> 00:02:05.929
they've interviewed
entrepreneurs, and they say,

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:08.904
"How important are
sales to your business?"

00:02:08.904 --> 00:02:11.893
And the entrepreneurs say, "Oh,
most important thing of all.

00:02:11.893 --> 00:02:13.653
"Oh, sales, blood to the brain,

00:02:13.653 --> 00:02:17.820
"oxygen to the heart, without
that, there's no business."

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.147
I say, okay, well, next
question the researchers ask is,

00:02:22.147 --> 00:02:24.381
"How much of your time
in the course of the day,

00:02:24.381 --> 00:02:27.680
"do you spend selling,
selling more stuff?"

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.368
And they say, "Oh, all
day long, that's all I do.

00:02:30.368 --> 00:02:31.354
"It's all I think about.

00:02:31.354 --> 00:02:33.709
"I get up in the morning,
think about it all day."

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:35.139
And so then they said, "Well, all right,

00:02:35.139 --> 00:02:36.473
"do you mind if we follow you around

00:02:36.473 --> 00:02:40.439
"with a camera and a
stopwatch for 30 days,

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:42.314
"and just see how you
actually use your time?"

00:02:42.314 --> 00:02:44.312
"No problem, no problem at all."

00:02:44.312 --> 00:02:45.590
You know what they found out?

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.151
The average entrepreneur
spends 11% of their time

00:02:48.151 --> 00:02:49.851
prospecting, presenting, and closing.

00:02:49.851 --> 00:02:50.840
- [Evan] Well, now.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.891
- The other 89% is spent, excuse

00:02:52.891 --> 00:02:54.969
the expression, dicking around.

00:02:54.969 --> 00:02:56.819
They're doing fun things, easy things,

00:02:56.819 --> 00:02:58.839
checking their email,
checking their email again,

00:02:58.839 --> 00:03:01.775
sending out emails, they
are making phone calls,

00:03:01.775 --> 00:03:05.689
they're checking their spam,
they are spending so much time.

00:03:05.689 --> 00:03:08.613
50% of working time today is wasted.

00:03:08.613 --> 00:03:09.874
And, if they're not checking email,

00:03:09.874 --> 00:03:11.178
they're chatting with their friends,

00:03:11.178 --> 00:03:12.305
and they're chatting with their buddies,

00:03:12.305 --> 00:03:14.913
and they're drinking coffee
and they're having lunch,

00:03:14.913 --> 00:03:17.557
and they're going around
feeling like big shots

00:03:17.557 --> 00:03:19.221
because they've got their own business.

00:03:19.221 --> 00:03:20.527
But, the fact of the matter is,

00:03:20.527 --> 00:03:22.970
if you're not prospecting,
presenting and closing,

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.206
you might as well go home to bed,

00:03:25.206 --> 00:03:27.146
because you're of no value, even worse,

00:03:27.146 --> 00:03:30.033
you're probably a
detriment to other people

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:33.124
'cause you're stopping them
from working by talking to them,

00:03:33.124 --> 00:03:35.878
or sending them email
or keeping them busy.

00:03:35.878 --> 00:03:38.718
Email, according to Harvard
University and throughout

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:42.695
three studies I read this
week, is killing entrepreneurs,

00:03:42.695 --> 00:03:45.738
'cause they can't stop,
they have this irresistible,

00:03:45.738 --> 00:03:47.246
almost like an addiction to

00:03:47.246 --> 00:03:50.083
electronic interruptions,
and they can't stop.

00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:51.782
And, so, just yesterday,
the Wall Street Journal

00:03:51.782 --> 00:03:55.143
had this great article which
is what I've been saying

00:03:55.143 --> 00:03:57.827
for the last five years, is turn it off.

00:03:57.827 --> 00:03:59.963
Don't turn it down, turn it off.

00:03:59.963 --> 00:04:03.202
Check it every two to three
hours, and then turn it off.

00:04:03.202 --> 00:04:05.327
"Oh, what if it's an important message?"

00:04:05.327 --> 00:04:06.688
Well, what you do is you say this,

00:04:06.688 --> 00:04:08.650
I check my email three times a day.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.107
If you've sent me an
email between those times,

00:04:11.107 --> 00:04:13.070
I will get back to you as soon as I can.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.732
If this is an emergency,
phone this number.

00:04:16.732 --> 00:04:19.534
And the phone will never ring.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:21.403
And then, what you do, is you

00:04:21.403 --> 00:04:23.584
do three 20-minute phases a day.

00:04:23.584 --> 00:04:26.920
First of all, your first
check is at 10:30 or 11:00,

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.482
you do not check your
email in the morning,

00:04:29.482 --> 00:04:31.277
because that immediately addicts you,

00:04:31.277 --> 00:04:33.073
and you're on email all day long.

00:04:33.073 --> 00:04:35.497
So, you wait 'till 10:30
or 11:00, check it once.

00:04:35.497 --> 00:04:38.039
Wait 'till two o'clock, check it again,

00:04:38.039 --> 00:04:39.990
wait 'till 4:30, check it the third time.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.735
On and off in 20 minutes and shut it down.

00:04:42.735 --> 00:04:43.722
If you can do that, you'll

00:04:43.722 --> 00:04:45.446
double and triple your productivity,

00:04:45.446 --> 00:04:48.333
and that's one of about a hundred
ideas that I can give you.

00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:50.983
But, if you'll just do
that, that'll do more

00:04:50.983 --> 00:04:54.888
to help you to be successful
in selling more stuff,

00:04:54.888 --> 00:04:57.479
because if you're not wasting
all this time doing that,

00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:00.250
you have only one choice
is to sell more stuff,

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.062
talk to customers, talk to people

00:05:02.062 --> 00:05:04.812
and ask them to buy your product.

